      "writtenOn": "2014-10-21T19:01:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible for toFile to exist when this code is called? I\u0027m asking because mkdir() will return *false* if it\u0027s called on an existing directory, so you normally write code like\n\n  if (!toFile.exists()) {\n      boolean ok \u003d toFile.mkdir();\n  }\n\n(Also, is it possible for any parent directories of toFile to not exist yet? If so, you might be safer with \"mkdirs\" instead of \"mkdir\".)",
      "revId": "0ab9b27265441d957a1ae405f1fcfb6358c2ed3a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
